Michal,

I have to apologize first off. I had IOMMU disabled in the bios and
neglected to double check before sending the last results. That has
been corrected, and I can assure you that I am on patch #2 and have
quadruple checked that IOMMU is enabled in the kernel and my BIOS.

Attached you will find dmesg from a cold boot, containing the "beef
cafe" string. Along with IOMMU groups being added as expected.
No faults were detected as far as I can tell.

>[    0.449289] xhci_hcd 0000:0c:00.0: beef cafe
>[   25.036180] xhci_hcd 0000:0c:00.0: Abort failed to stop command ring: -=
110
>[   25.036189] xhci_hcd 0000:0c:00.0: xHCI host controller not responding,=
 assume dead
>[   25.036192] xhci_hcd 0000:0c:00.0: HC died; cleaning up

>[    0.364927] AMD-Vi: Extended features (0x246577efa2254afa, 0x0): PPR NX=
 GT [5] IA GA PC GA_vAPIC
>[    0.364934] AMD-Vi: Interrupt remapping enabled
>[    0.457869] AMD-Vi: Virtual APIC enabled

ERSTBA LOW contained 'beef'. ERSTBA HIGH was zeroed out. (pulled from slot_=
200)

>IR0_ERSTSZ     =3D 0x00000002
>IR0_ERSTBA_LOW =3D 0xbeef0000
>IR0_ERSTBA_HIGH =3D 0x00000000
>IR0_ERDP_LOW   =3D 0xffffd000
>IR0_ERDP_HIGH  =3D 0x00000000

I'm seeing 0c:00.0 in IOMMU group 18. Default domain as Translated.

>readlink /sys/bus/pci/devices/0000:0c:00.0/iommu_group
>../../../../../../../../../../kernel/iommu_groups/18

>cat /sys/kernel/iommu_groups/18/type
 >sudo dmesg | grep -i "IOMMU DMA protection is disabled"
 >sudo dmesg | grep -iE "Default domain|domain type|identity|DMA-FQ"
 >DMA-FQ
 >[   29.656955] thunderbolt 0000:09:00.0: IOMMU DMA protection is disabled
 >[    0.336442] iommu: Default domain type: Translated

Sorry for the delay this time.

Best,
Ben




